# warnings

## UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE

```text
[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] `import defer` of the external module "ext" is lowered to a normal import in IIFE output, because the module is a global or a wrapper argument. The module evaluates when the bundle starts, not at the first access to its namespace.
   ╭─[ main.js:1:1 ]
   │
 1 │ import defer * as ns from 'ext';
   │ ────────────────┬───────────────  
   │                 ╰───────────────── 
───╯

```

## UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE

```text
[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] `import.defer()` of the external module "ext2" is lowered to `import()` in IIFE output. The module evaluates when the `import()` call loads it, not at the first access to its namespace.
   ╭─[ main.js:4:27 ]
   │
 4 │ export const load = () => import.defer('ext2');
   │                           ──────────┬─────────  
   │                                     ╰─────────── 
───╯

```

# Assets

## main.js

```js
var lib = (function(exports, ext) {
	Object.defineProperty(exports, Symbol.toStringTag, { value: "Module" });
	// HIDDEN [\0rolldown/runtime.js]
	ext = __toESM(ext);
	// main.js
	const read = () => ext.value;
	const load = () => import("ext2");
	exports.load = load;
	exports.read = read;
	return exports;
})({}, Ext);

```

